        *   Expected Output: `https://example.com`
        *   Explanation: `subdomainPrefixRegex.MatchString("evil://attacker.com")` will return `false` because `:` and `/` are not allowed. The `isValidSubdomainPrefix` flag will be `false`, leading to the default URL.

